    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39785" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pyrrhĭcha</span></b> , ae, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pyrrhĭchē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρριχη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a dance in
			armor</i>, <i>the Pyrrhic dance</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56,
				57, § 204</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">elephas lasciviente pyrrhiche conludere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					2, 2, § 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Ner. 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Spart. Hadr 19</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 253,
			18</span></i>.—As adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ars pyrrhicha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 15, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
